<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! engine.record.removes ~ a delete by the family law, plain unless a lower layer makes it a choice

A delete deletes plainly: with no `mode`, each record leaves its own layer to absent and no tombstone rises (the receipt reads `mode: "plain"` and names each title under `retracted`). `base` carries the hash last read: a record that moved past it moves nothing and answers `conflict`, naming the live hash. A title the wiki reads absent answers `absent`, and a plain delete there retracts a kāpae that hides nothing (its `.kapae` shadow leaves the disk). The address stays a candidate until the operator reads the landing's list.

The family law decides what moves, read over the reader's view before anything lands. A plain tiddler leaves alone. A meme root answers the consequence the delete would land (every title it would move, what it would leave) and refuses `tiddler-delete-in-a-family` unless `family` names the family act, which lands the root and its slots as one change per layer (the answer adds `canonicalHash`). A slot's title (`<root>#/x`) leaves as the explicit cut on its parent, and the family reseals.

Only a lower layer makes a delete a choice. A wiki composes layers (canon under working under personal), and one title may stand in several. Where a lower layer holds the title too, or the record rests in a layer this face cannot remove it from, a delete naming no mode refuses `delete-mode-needed` and names both meanings: `mode` kapae raises a tombstone in a writable layer that shadows every record beneath (the wiki reads the title gone, the lower layers keep theirs); `mode` reveal retracts the topmost record so the one beneath surfaces, refusing `reveal-top-unwritable` where the face cannot write that layer. Each act in `consequence.acts` names `bag` (the layer written), `holds` (every layer holding the title) and what the wiki reads afterward: `shadowed: [bags]` or `reveals: bag | null`.

A rendered tiddler (one carrying `rendered-from`) refuses `rendered-derives`: only the renderer writes it, and it leaves when its source drops `projection: rendered`. A `$:/` title refuses too. `recipe` removes through that wiki's engine; `bag` removes from that one bag through its store, `family` taking the family there too. A delete writes the face it wears and never another (`cross-face-write-refused`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ a-plain-delete · a-family · reveal · kapae · one-bag

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-plain-delete` params=`title/[[Old Note]] recipe/default base/<hash> ~ the record leaves; a stale base moves nothing`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-family` params=`title/lar:///ha.ka.ba/kahua/memory/x recipe/default family/true ~ a meme root and its slots, one change`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`reveal` params=`title/[[Room 4]] recipe/default mode/reveal ~ drop my copy; the layer beneath surfaces`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`kapae` params=`title/[[Room 4]] recipe/default mode/kapae ~ hide the title; the layers beneath keep theirs`>>
<<has entity=`example` name=`one-bag` params=`title/[[Old Note]] bag/notes ~ that one bag's record leaves through its store`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ title · container · face · base · family · mode · mu

<<~ kahea uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance#/takes/container`>>
<<~ kahea uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance#/takes/face`>>
<<~ kahea uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/affordance#/takes/mu`>>

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`mu` params=`takes/carry skins/console,cli default/?0 ~ the lens; this door's default reads ?0 (cup), the receipt's has line`>>
<<has entity=`cell` name=`?0` params=`mu/cup ~ the receipt: the delete lands and answers its has line, the default`>>
<<has entity=`cell` name=`!0` params=`mu/sword ~ the receipt asserted: the delete lands and a terminal prints the machine answer verbatim`>>
<<has entity=`cell` name=`_0` params=`mu/pentacle ~ a dry run: the delete walks its law to the last step and answers the summary, landing nothing`>>
<<has entity=`cell` name=`_?` params=`mu/overview ~ the dry summary: what the delete would land, the bag and layer, the base it needs, landing nothing`>>
<<has entity=`cell` name=`_!` params=`mu/precision ~ the dry diff: the summary and each record it would move, fields before and after and text line by line, landing nothing`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`title` params=`takes/title needs/required seat/1 as/<title> ~ the record removed; a slot title <root>#/x leaves as the cut on its parent`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`base` params=`takes/hash ~ the hash last read; a stale one answers conflict and nothing moves`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`family` params=`~ name the family act: a meme root leaves with its slots, one change`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`mode` params=`takes/kapae-or-reveal ~ over a lower layer's record: kapae hides it, reveal surfaces it; none, a plain delete`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

